From 0fdf3cc4490f62706c8b28d191f7933ba4be271f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atlas agent <agent@atlas.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:08:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] window: REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW_COMPOSITOR_FILE moves the windows
 to another Wayland compositor, no restart

The file names a Wayland socket. The UI thread connects to it itself, hands SDL the connection
(SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_WL_DISPLAY_POINTER) and holds SDL's events apart from its video.
When the file names another socket, each window lets its input go and hides, and its render thread
lets the swapchain and surface go (a new detach handshake, beside close/released). Once the last SDL
window is gone, SDL's video restarts on the new connection and the windows open there. The displays,
their sinks and the guest are untouched. On failure the windows go back to the old compositor.
<file>.on says where they are. Unset, nothing changes.

Off-Tahoe check (SDL 3.4.18, two sway 1.12, lavapipe): 100 moves in one process, first present
2-18 ms after a move starts, fds constant. Not yet verified on ANV/dmabuf or with input.
